    <ReasonableCauseExplanation documentId="R000004" softwareId="23018249" softwareVersionNum="v1.00">
      <ExplanationTxt>I respectfully ask the IRS to consider this late filing as the result of a misunderstanding on my part. After filing Form 990-N (e-Postcard) for the 2022 tax year, I mistakenly believed that small nonprofits with gross receipts under $50,000 were only required to file every two years. Based on this misunderstanding, I did not submit a return for 2023 on time. Once I realized my mistake, I took immediate steps to correct the issue by preparing and submitting Form 990-EZ for the 2023 tax year. I now understand that annual filing is required, regardless of revenue level, and I am fully committed to remaining in compliance going forward. I respectfully request that any penalties for late filing be waived, as this was an honest mistake made in good faith, and I acted promptly to correct it.</ExplanationTxt>
    </ReasonableCauseExplanation>
